  "id": "Compound::DB00777 - Gene::147",
  "verbalization": "Propiomazine is shown to bind to Adra1d, a variant of the Adra1 receptor, which is involved in Alpha1-adrenergic receptor activity. This activity is then participated in by Adra1b, suggesting a potential role for Propiomazine in modulating the function of Adra1b. The evidence from multiple paths indicates that Propiomazine interacts with Adra1d, which is functionally linked to Adra1b, implying a possible mechanism by which Propiomazine influences Adra1b activity. The overlapping pathways highlight a shared involvement of Adra1d and Adra1b in Alpha-adrenergic signaling, suggesting that Propiomazine may act through a common pathway involving these receptors. The integration of these findings supports a hypothesis that Propiomazine exerts its effects by interacting with Adra1d, which in turn modulates Adra1b activity, potentially through a mechanism involving Alpha-adrenergic receptor signaling.",
